Creating First GitOps Application

✨ Hello DevOps Learners!
Continuing my GitOps learning journey after completing Ansible, today I’m creating my first GitOps application using Argo CD 🚀
This is where GitOps becomes real — deploying applications directly from Git to Kubernetes.

🔹 Step 1 — Git Repo + YAML Deployment
 First, we create a Git repository that contains:
Kubernetes YAML manifests
Deployment configuration files
Service definitions

Example:

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: my-app
spec:
  replicas: 2

This repository defines the desired state of the application.

🔹 Step 2 — Create Application in ArgoCD
 Using ArgoCD UI or CLI:
Connect your Git repository
Specify the Kubernetes cluster and namespace
Define the path to YAML files
ArgoCD now understands what to deploy and where.

🔹 Step 3 — Sync Application
Click Sync in UI or use CLI
ArgoCD compares Git (desired state) with cluster (actual state)
It applies changes to match the desired configuration

🔹 Step 4 — Auto Deployment
 Once configured, ArgoCD can:
Automatically detect Git changes
Deploy updates without manual steps
Keep the system continuously in sync

💡 Key Insight:
 GitOps allows you to deploy applications just by updating Git, making deployments automated, reliable, and version-controlled.
